<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left breast cancer, pathologic stage IIA (pT1c pN1a), after mastectomy and axillary dissection (C50.122)</content>. Healing well. Grade 3, node-positive, hormone receptor-positive disease in a man of 51, for which chemotherapy followed by tamoxifen is the standard plan. Blood count, kidney, and liver function allow full-dose chemotherapy. [S]<list><item>Echocardiogram this week before doxorubicin.</item><item>Preventive visit next week for vaccines and hepatitis B screening before chemotherapy; dental check before the first cycle.</item><item>Continue shoulder exercises; a physical therapy session if movement has not returned by the first cycle.</item><item>Sperm banking offered by oncology before chemotherapy; his decision is with them.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Estrogen receptor-positive status (Z17.0)</content>. Tamoxifen after chemotherapy for at least five years; an aromatase inhibitor alone is not used in men. [S]<list><item>Tamoxifen safety monitoring to start with treatment: clot symptoms, mood, hot flashes, sexual side effects, and adherence.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Blood count before chemotherapy</td><td>Before cycle 1 and each cycle (oncology)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hemoglobin 13.9 g/dL, white cells 7.0, neutrophils 4.3, platelets 281</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Kidney and liver function before chemotherapy</td><td>Before cycle 1 (oncology)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 0.98 mg/dL, eGFR 93; ALT 21 U/L, bilirubin 0.6 mg/dL, albumin 4.3 g/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram with ejection fraction before anthracycline</td><td>Baseline before doxorubicin</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked this week</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hepatitis B screening before chemotherapy</td><td>Before the first cycle</td><td>Due</td><td>To be drawn at the preventive visit next week</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Germline multigene panel testing</td><td>Once, for every man with breast cancer</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Sent fifteen days ago; result not yet back</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Wound and shoulder movement after axillary surgery</td><td>Each visit after surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Healed; flexion 150 degrees, improving</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lymphedema assessment and risk-reduction counseling</td><td>Every visit after axillary surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Upper arm circumference 33.5 cm on both sides; skin care, avoiding tight sleeves on the left arm, and early reporting of swelling taught</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Baseline arm circumference missed before surgery</td><td>Once, before axillary surgery</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not measured before the operation, a deviation from the protocol. Measured today at thirteen days, before any swelling, and equal on both sides; the right arm serves as the reference. No harm is evident, and future measurements will be compared with today&apos;s</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>Each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 6, mild; no thoughts of self-harm; peer support and counseling offered</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Tamoxifen safety (clot symptoms, mood, hot flashes, sexual side effects, adherence)</td><td>Every visit once tamoxifen starts</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Tamoxifen starts after chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Mammography</td><td>Yearly only for a breast treated by lumpectomy, or the other breast with a predisposing variant</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No breast was treated by lumpectomy. Imaging of the other side is considered only with a predisposing variant, and the germline result is pending</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking daily; gym work for the legs; no heavy lifting with the left arm for another two weeks</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Tissue diagnosis within one week of presentation. Outcome by 1993-10-05: Imaging and core biopsy the day after presentation; diagnosis explained on the sixth day [S]</item><item>Curative surgery within two weeks of diagnosis, with lymphedema prevention taught. Outcome by 1993-10-20: Mastectomy and axillary dissection two days after the diagnosis; clear margins; arm exercises and risk reduction taught [S]</item><item>Complete germline genetic testing with counseling before chemotherapy starts. In progress; target 1993-10-27 [S]</item><item>Be ready to start adjuvant chemotherapy within six weeks of surgery: echocardiogram, hepatitis B screening, vaccines, and dental review done. In progress; target 1993-10-27 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Armenian SH, et al. Prevention and Monitoring of Cardiac Dysfunction in Survivors of Adult Cancers: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2017;35(8):893-911 (2017); Hwang JP, et al. Hepatitis B Virus Screening and Management for Patients With Cancer Prior to Therapy: ASCO Provisional Clinical Opinion Update. J Clin Oncol 2020 (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Echocardiogram this week. Preventive visit next week. Chemotherapy in about two weeks with medical oncology. Primary care review during chemotherapy. Next scheduled visit 1993-10-27: periodic adult preventive visit before chemotherapy. [S]</paragraph></text>

